<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk set for Oct 21-24 repairs.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk set for Oct 21-24 repairs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The leading Russian Black Sea oil export terminal Novorossiisk is expected to close during four days of pipeline maintenance later in October, shipping and trading sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Maintenance on the main pipeline supplying the 650,000 barrels per day (bpd) terminal is tentatively scheduled for October 21-24, the sources said.</p>
<p>But they said the schedule was likely to be subject to rearrangement at short notice.</p>
<p>--Richard Mably, London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
